age from which there's no  escaping  but the process wouldn't quite end there  some of the stixxosaurus fossils were  found with over 200 small stones in  their bellies  these stones could have served as a  ballast helping the prehistoric  creatures sink closer to the ocean floor  but it's more likely that the rocks  aided with digestion  yeah while the teeth of the stixxosaurus  evolved for seizing slippery prey  they weren't particularly effective at  cutting through flesh  so this behemoth would swallow its  still-living prey whole  and the stones in its belly would take  care of crushing bones and rubbing off  scales  now if it set its eyes on you would you  end up rocking and rolling in its  stomach  well  the head of an average stixxasaurus  would be around 50 centimeters long with  a snout of about 30 centimeters in  length  that means if you happen to be an  average sized adult this sea reptile  wouldn't want to try swallowing you  whole  you wouldn't fit in its mouth  now if stixxasaurus could swallow you  whole you'd experience a sudden  inescapable darkness as you slide down a  long neck and land in a stone pit  and that's where you'd finally be  pummeled to death with rocks  what a bizarre way to go  it's a good thing this behemoth wouldn't  be big enough to swallow you in one  piece  but this doesn't mean you'd go  completely unharmed  the stixxosaurus might be trying to take  a bite out of you in self-defense  your best bet for surviving would be to  do what you would do during a shark  attack  the worst thing you could do is panic  and splash around  that would only peak the stixxosaurus's  curiosity  instead try to look as big and  intimidating as you possibly can  of course that's easier said than done  when facing a predator 45 times your  size  if you managed to gain the  stixxosaurus's respect and it left you  alone  it could settle for the smaller portion  options  but sticking to fish and squid would  make it run into some fierce competition  n